        "kit_category_YcM36D": {
          "type": "kit_category",
          "settings": {
            "header": "{{ page.metafields.custom.instructions_included_header_2.value }}What This Kit Does",
            "body": "<p>This kit swaps your factory JL/JT electric power steering setup for a belt-driven pump. Why? Because real steering needs real power — and PSC delivers.</p>"
          }
        },
        "kit_category_whAfV7": {
          "type": "kit_category",
          "settings": {
            "header": "{{ page.metafields.custom.instructions_included_header_4.value }}Before You Start",
            "body": "<p>Park on a flat surface, set the brake, and disconnect the battery. &nbsp;<br/>If you’re also installing a Big Bore XD steering gear, grab a helper. That gear weighs about 50 lbs and is awkward to thread in alone.<br/>Protect paint when you lean the hood back.<br/>If you’re not comfortable with the job, no shame in letting a pro handle it.</p>"
          }
        },
        "kit_category_iMq7aX": {
          "type": "kit_category",
          "settings": {
            "header": "What’s in the Kit",
            "body": "<p>Major Components:</p><ul><li>SP33362S-3558 – Power Steering Pump, LHD CBR, 16MM Pressure, ‑12AN Feed</li><li>SR300MK – Power Steering Fluid Reservoir Kit – Jeep JL/JT 3.6L (Non‑eTorque)</li><li>CK220 – Jeep JL/JT 3.6L Power Steering Cooler Kit</li><li>MB12K – Power Steering Pump Mount Kit – Jeep Gladiator 3.6L Pentastar</li></ul><p>Drive System:</p><ul><li>BT60905 – 6‑Rib Serpentine Drive Belt – 90.5”</li></ul><p>Hose System:</p><ul><li>HMK‑PK1880 – Master Hose Kit:<br/>H-THS-1.8ML-VT — Vibra-Tite 440 Anaerobic Pneumatic / Hydraulic Thread &nbsp; &nbsp; Sealant (1.8 mL Tube)</li><li>HA-L104 — Drain Hose Assembly – Remote Reservoir</li><li>HK2094 – High‑Pressure Hose Assembly – JL/JT 3.6L (PSC Pump Kits Only)</li><li>HA-L103 — Hose Assembly – Remote Fill to Reservoir</li><li>HA-L102 — Hose Assembly – Remote Reservoir to Pump</li></ul><p>Fluids:</p><ul><li>FL‑SWE715‑4PAK – PSC 715 Power Steering Fluid – 4 Quart Pack<br/><br/></li></ul>"
          }
        },
        "kit_category_PbdGtb": {
          "type": "kit_category",
          "settings": {
            "header": "Tools You’ll Need",
            "body": "<ul><li>Standard hand tools</li><li>8 mm, 10 mm sockets</li><li>Torque wrench (up to 225 ft‑lb)</li><li>46 mm socket (for Big Bore gear)</li><li>Drill and cut‑off tool (for isolator trim)</li><li>Hose clamp pliers and zip ties</li><li>To finish the conversion, you’ll need to delete the electric steering mode in the ECU. We use and sell the Tazer JL Programmer. You can grab it from PSC or most Jeep aftermarket dealers.</li></ul>"
          }
        },
        "step_K6k3PQ": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "image_position": "split",
            "header": "STEP",
            "label": "Get Access",
            "body": "<p>{{ page.metafields.custom.step_1_content | metafield_tag }}Some bumper/winch setups sit tight to the grille. If yours does, removing it now will make the install a lot easier.<br/></p>",
            "image_1": "shopify://shop_images/step_1.webp"
          }
        },
        "step_p4UDTU": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "image_position": "right",
            "header": "STEP",
            "label": "{{ page.metafields.custom.instructions_step_2.value }}Hood",
            "body": "<p>{{ page.metafields.custom.step_2_content | metafield_tag }}Lean the hood back against the windshield.<br/></p><p><strong>Tip:</strong> Put something soft between them so you don’t scratch the paint or glass.<br/></p>",
            "image_1": "shopify://shop_images/step_2.webp"
          }
        },
        "step_mPKCht": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "image_position": "right",
            "header": "STEP",
            "label": "{{ page.metafields.custom.instructions_step_3.value }}Air System",
            "body": "<p>Disconnect the battery.&nbsp;</p><p>Remove the air filter assembly and intake tubing.</p>",
            "image_1": "shopify://shop_images/step_3_b660ac4c-6d82-4e89-a759-0fd37c1afd91.webp"
          }
        },
        "step_Ti9JPh": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "image_position": "split",
            "header": "STEP",
            "label": "Fresh Air Inlet",
            "body": "<p>Remove the fresh air inlet tubing.</p>",
            "image_1": "shopify://shop_images/step_4_a1b4cdac-5375-4f60-9997-7e5f42b1b7ae.webp"
          }
        },
        "step_g4dyXM": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "image_position": "left",
            "header": "STEP",
            "label": "{{ page.metafields.custom.instructions_step_5.value }}Fenders & Inner Wells",
            "body": "<p>Remove both fenders with inner wells as one piece: (4) bolts and (1) push pin. Start at the rear and pull up/out.<br/></p><p><strong>Tip</strong>: Mopar clips can break — &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; replacements are easy to find (Part# 6852‑6185‑AA‑008).<br/></p>",
            "image_1": "shopify://shop_images/step_5_0cfed037-da06-448c-be30-b4b567ea2a1e.webp"
          }
        },
        "step_dnDcgn": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "image_position": "right",
            "header": "STEP",
            "label": "Wiring at Fender",
            "body": "<p>Before the fender comes off, disconnect the light connector.</p><p>Slide the red lock tab, press the black tab, and pull apart.<br/></p>",
            "image_1": "shopify://shop_images/step_5a_9e3c83dc-a52b-4739-80c1-6ca9c136889a.webp"
          }
        },
        "step_xkAxXJ": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "image_position": "right",
            "header": "STEP",
            "label": "Grille",
            "body": "<p>Pop the (6) push rivets along the top.&nbsp;</p><p>Pull the bottom edge to release snap connectors.</p>",
            "image_1": "shopify://shop_images/step_6_9fff4c74-37f6-4f73-9929-571364b886c5.webp"
          }
        },
        "step_Mw8NCM": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "image_position": "right",
            "header": "STEP",
            "label": "{{ page.metafields.custom.instructions_step_7.value }}Vacuum Pump",
            "body": "<p>Remove (2) 8 mm bolts at the bottom of the alternator bracket.&nbsp;<br/></p><p>Disconnect the line clamps and move the pump out of the way.<br/></p>",
            "image_1": "shopify://shop_images/step_7.webp"
          }
        },
        "step_V3gA8w": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "image_position": "right",
            "header": "STEP",
            "label": "Belt Tensioner",
            "body": "<p>Release the tensioner and remove the belt from the idler pulley. The OE belt comes off completely in the next step.<br/></p>",
            "image_1": "shopify://shop_images/step_8.webp"
          }
        },
        "step_ffDf7T": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "image_position": "right",
            "header": "STEP",
            "label": "Install PSC Pump & Belt",
            "body": "<p>Disconnect the alternator and bracket by removing the (3) 10 mm bolts and (1) 8 mm bolt.&nbsp;<br/></p><p>Lay the alternator and bracket back out of the way, and secure it with a bungee cord or strap if needed.<br/></p><p>Remove the OE belt and discard it.</p><p><em>Tip: Sketch the OE belt route for reference.</em><br/></p>",
            "image_1": "shopify://shop_images/step_9.webp"
          }
        },
        "step_qHpddh": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "image_position": "right",
            "header": "STEP",
            "label": "Steering Gear Lines",
            "body": "<p>Disconnect pressure and return lines from the steering gear.<br/></p>",
            "image_1": "shopify://shop_images/step_10.webp"
          }
        },
        "step_Y3Vxd7": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "image_position": "right",
            "header": "STEP",
            "label": "OE Pump",
            "body": "<p>Disconnect wiring harnesses plus pressure/return lines from the OE pump. Remove the (2) mount bolts (save one for reuse) and remove the OE power steering pump.</p>",
            "image_1": "shopify://shop_images/step_11.webp"
          }
        },
        "step_kNUzab": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "image_position": "right",
            "header": "STEP",
            "label": "Lines Between Pump & Steering Gear",
            "body": "<p>Lines Between Pump & Steering Gear</p>",
            "image_1": "shopify://shop_images/step_12.webp"
          }
        },
        "step_8XM3YY": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "image_position": "split",
            "header": "STEP",
            "label": "Lines Between Pump & Steering Gear",
            "body": "<p>Remove the OE power steering fluid fill reservoir.<br/></p>",
            "image_1": "shopify://shop_images/step_13.webp"
          }
        },
        "step_cHqj7f": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "image_position": "split",
            "header": "STEP",
            "label": "Motor Mounts & Idler",
            "body": "<p>Loosen the top motor mount nut on the driver side until it’s almost off.&nbsp;<br/></p><p>Remove the same nut on the &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; passenger side. Remove the OE idler pulley assembly.<br/></p>",
            "image_1": "shopify://shop_images/step_14.webp"
          }
        },
        "step_byGprp": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "image_position": "right",
            "header": "STEP",
            "label": "Support the Engine",
            "body": "<p>Support the engine with a wooden block under the oil pan and lift ½–1”<br/></p><p><strong>Important</strong>: Do not lift more than ~1”. Watch firewall clearance.<br/></p>",
            "image_1": "{{ page.metafields.custom.instructions_step_15_image.value }}",
            "image_2": "shopify://shop_images/step_15.webp"
          }
        },
        "step_rhGMA9": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "image_position": "right",
            "header": "STEP",
            "label": "OE Aluminum Mount",
            "body": "<p>Remove the (4) bolts holding the OE aluminum mount to the engine block.&nbsp;</p><p>Remove the mount.</p>",
            "image_1": "shopify://shop_images/step_16.webp"
          }
        },
        "step_CeQMB4": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "image_position": "right",
            "header": "STEP",
            "label": "Isolator Trim",
            "body": "<p>Trim the corner of the frame‑mounted engine isolator as shown. A cut‑off tool works fine.</p>",
            "image_1": "shopify://shop_images/step_17.webp"
          }
        },
        "step_e66zbV": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "image_position": "split",
            "header": "STEP",
            "label": "PSC Bracket (12.12)",
            "body": "<p>Install the PSC 12.12 mount in reverse order. Lower the engine and tighten isolator mount bolts.</p>",
            "image_1": "{{ page.metafields.custom.instructions_step_18_image.value }}",
            "image_2": "shopify://shop_images/step_18.webp"
          }
        },
        "step_AnjD4q": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "image_position": "right",
            "header": "STEP",
            "label": "Pump & Belt",
            "body": "<p>Install the PSC pump using the (2) 5/16‑18×3” bolts with flat washers.&nbsp;</p><p><br/>Route the BT60900 belt.&nbsp;</p><p><br/>Reinstall the alternator/bracket &nbsp; &nbsp; (belt over alternator pulley first).</p><p><br/>Release the tensioner and seat the belt on all pulleys. Reinstall the vacuum pump.</p><p><br/><strong>Note</strong>: Belt routing is the same as OE. PSC pump takes the idler pulley’s spot.<br/></p>",
            "image_1": "shopify://shop_images/step_19.webp"
          }
        },
        "step_GtfRgX": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "image_position": "split",
            "header": "STEP",
            "label": "High‑Pressure Hose (HK2094)",
            "body": "<p>Route HK2094 below the radiator, in front of the crossmember, and up to the pump and gearbox.&nbsp;</p><p><br/>Loosely install the (2) HCL‑12‑13 clamps.&nbsp;</p><p><br/>Do not tighten them until both hose ends are connected and fully &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; tightened.</p>",
            "image_1": "shopify://shop_images/step_20.webp"
          }
        },
        "step_Dxa9J7": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "image_position": "right",
            "header": "STEP",
            "label": "Steering Gear Fittings",
            "body": "<p>Install SF01‑HF fitting in the pressure port and connect HK2094.</p>",
            "image_1": "shopify://shop_images/step_22.png"
          }
        },
        "step_wbGbH3": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "image_position": "right",
            "header": "STEP",
            "label": "Pump Connection (leave loose)",
            "body": "<p>Connect the other end of the HK2094 hose to the pump. Don’t tighten yet.</p>"
          }
        },
        "step_kz8YVT": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "image_position": "right",
            "header": "STEP",
            "label": "Reservoir Supply Hose",
            "body": "<p>Pre‑assemble HA‑L102 to the frame‑mounted reservoir. Don’t clamp yet.</p>"
          }
        },
        "step_xJck3g": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "image_position": "right",
            "header": "STEP",
            "label": "Mount Reservoir & Tie to Pump",
            "body": "<p>Start the supply hose fitting on the pump first.&nbsp;</p><p><br/>Mount the reservoir using (1) OE bolt in front and (1) 8‑1.25×100 mm bolt with flat washer in the rear.&nbsp;</p><p><br/>Tighten fittings at power steering pump, compress clamp, and slide onto hose at reservoir connection.</p>",
            "image_1": "shopify://shop_images/step_24.png"
          }
        },
        "step_6rgHA6": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "image_position": "right",
            "header": "STEP",
            "label": "Secure Hose Clamp",
            "body": "<p>Fasten HA‑H200 hose clamp to the rear reservoir mount bolt with lock nut and washer.&nbsp;</p><p>Tighten the hose fitting at the pump.</p>",
            "image_1": "shopify://shop_images/step_25.png"
          }
        },
        "step_npw68w": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "image_position": "right",
            "header": "STEP",
            "label": "Remote Fill Hose (HA‑L103)",
            "body": "<p>Connect HA‑L103 to the fill reservoir. Clock the fitting as shown and tighten.</p><p>Route hose toward the firewall, loop forward, and connect to the main reservoir.</p>",
            "image_1": "shopify://shop_images/step_26.png"
          }
        },
        "step_gNJhBM": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "image_position": "right",
            "header": "STEP",
            "label": "Mount the Fill Reservoir",
            "body": "<p>Install fill reservoir under the bracket tab using (1) ¼‑20×1” bolt, flat &nbsp; &nbsp;washer, and lock nut.</p>"
          }
        },
        "step_zgNyRE": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "image_position": "right",
            "header": "STEP",
            "label": "Anti‑Splash Valve (SR‑VT)",
            "body": "<p>Mount SR‑VT on the driver‑side bracket.</p><ul><li>If your bracket has a welded nut, use (1) 6‑1.0×25 mm flange bolt.</li><li>If not, use a 6 mm bolt with lock nut.<br/></li></ul>",
            "image_1": "shopify://shop_images/step_28.png"
          }
        },
        "step_GUYWhE": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "image_position": "right",
            "header": "STEP",
            "label": "Vent Line",
            "body": "<p>Push ¼” tubing into SR‑VT’s push‑lock fitting.</p><p>Route along the top of the radiator under the plastic guard and connect to the fill reservoir.</p><p></p>"
          }
        },
        "step_yUJ9zw": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "image_position": "right",
            "header": "STEP",
            "label": "Cooler & Final Hoses",
            "body": "<p>Install cooler fittings from the CMK212S-8TN bag with thread sealant.</p><p>Mount the cooler to the cooler bracket using the t-slot nuts and bolts in the &nbsp;CMK212S-8TN bag.</p><p>Mount the cooler using the provided bolts/self tapping screws found in the HWK-CK220 bag&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Steering Gear → Cooler HA-L151</li><li>Cooler → Reservoir HA-L152</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>Note:</strong> Go through the entire system and make sure thread sealant was used everywhere it’s required, and confirm all fittings are fully tightened.<br/>Your final step is to follow the fill and bleed procedures to get all the air out of the steering system for best performance.</p>",
            "image_1": "shopify://shop_images/step_30.png"
          }
        }
      },
